WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.270
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Sunday, November eighth.

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.083
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:11.727
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:13.270
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:23.013
UK maritime authorities have issued two time-late tanker warnings near the Strait of Hormuz, and the US military says it disabled a cargo ship in the Gulf of Oman.

6
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:28.421
In Riyadh, an Aramco building was damaged by falling debris after an attempted attack.

7
00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:30.957
Here's the detail.

8
00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:31.905
Gulf shipping.

9
00:00:31.905 --> 00:00:45.245
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations, warning one ninety-nine: a time-late report that a tanker was on fire about eight nautical miles off northern Oman on Saturday afternoon, Central time, and that the crew were evacuated.

10
00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.422
Military authorities were the source.

11
00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:54.050
UKMTO listed this as suspicious activity, not as a confirmed attack, and did not state a cause.

12
00:00:54.050 --> 00:01:04.339
Separately, warning two hundred, also a time-late report: a tanker sailing outbound through the Strait of Hormuz was struck by an unknown projectile about an hour later.

13
00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:10.124
The company security officer said all crew were safe and there was no reported environmental impact.

14
00:01:10.124 --> 00:01:13.328
UKMTO classed that incident as an attack.

15
00:01:13.328 --> 00:01:14.797
Reporting can lag.

16
00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:19.416
These are two separate warnings, and Tueri is not treating them as the same ship.

17
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:27.073
Also confirmed: advisory one ninety-eight reports an incident involving a bulk carrier and military forces in the Gulf of Oman, about eighteen nautical miles off the UAE's east coast.

18
00:01:27.073 --> 00:01:30.773
Crew status and damage are unknown.

19
00:01:30.773 --> 00:01:43.536
Separately, confirmed by US Central Command: it disabled a Saint Kitts-flagged cargo ship in the Gulf of Oman on Saturday after the civilian crew ignored repeated warnings and tried to leave the region after visiting an Iranian port.

20
00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.879
A US aircraft fired on the ship's stern.

21
00:01:46.879 --> 00:01:52.334
CENTCOM did not give a precise position, and UKMTO did not name the vessel.

22
00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:59.802
The latest joint maritime centre assessment still rates the Strait of Hormuz severe and the wider Arabian Gulf substantial.

23
00:01:59.802 --> 00:02:08.443
Tueri suggests operators review routing and crew-welfare plans for Gulf and Gulf of Oman voyages, and treat unmatched claims as unconfirmed.

24
00:02:08.443 --> 00:02:11.251
Saudi Arabia.

25
00:02:11.251 --> 00:02:19.052
Reported, through the Saudi energy ministry: an administrative building belonging to Aramco in Riyadh was damaged by falling debris after an attempted attack on Sunday.

26
00:02:19.052 --> 00:02:22.516
The ministry said the damage was limited and that no one was hurt.

27
00:02:22.516 --> 00:02:29.772
A Reuters journalist saw blown-out windows across several floors of the tower in the city's financial district.

28
00:02:29.772 --> 00:02:35.178
Reported, through the Saudi-led coalition: air defenses intercepted missiles aimed at Riyadh and other regions.

29
00:02:35.178 --> 00:02:42.270
Saudi civil defense issued and later lifted alerts in Riyadh and in parts of the Eastern Province.

30
00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:47.436
There was no immediate Houthi claim of responsibility for the Riyadh building damage.

31
00:02:47.436 --> 00:02:57.214
At about two forty-five p.m. local time, Flightradar twenty-four showed eleven Riyadh cancellations, about five percent, against roughly two hundred nine flights on the board.

32
00:02:57.214 --> 00:03:03.156
That is a different board from Saturday's afternoon check, so no trend can be drawn.

33
00:03:03.156 --> 00:03:08.600
The US Mission security alert of Saturday still stands; no newer mission alert was found.

34
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:14.497
Tueri suggests travelers confirm each flight with the airline and keep a ground route in their contingency plans.

35
00:03:14.497 --> 00:03:17.295
Europe.

36
00:03:17.295 --> 00:03:24.514
Confirmed by the State Department and Britain's Foreign Office: there was a shooting in Krakow's main square on Saturday.

37
00:03:24.514 --> 00:03:27.246
Local police say the suspect is in custody.

38
00:03:27.246 --> 00:03:30.014
Follow local instructions if you are in the area.

39
00:03:30.014 --> 00:03:38.869
Separately, the State Department says a general strike is still set across Spain on Wednesday, November eleventh, with transport cut to minimum services.

40
00:03:38.869 --> 00:03:43.169
Britain's Foreign Office has not yet updated its Spain page for the strike.

41
00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:48.489
Tueri suggests travelers allow extra time and confirm any Wednesday travel in Spain.

42
00:03:48.489 --> 00:03:49.983
Operations check.

43
00:03:49.983 --> 00:03:58.956
Borders and health, US: the Ebola attestation order remains in force for flights to the United States, with no change on the CDC page.

44
00:03:58.956 --> 00:04:00.355
No attestation, no boarding.

45
00:04:00.355 --> 00:04:06.818
Borders and health, Nigeria: travelers could be subject to quarantine or self-isolation for at least twenty-one days.

46
00:04:06.818 --> 00:04:10.426
That describes a possibility, not a blanket rule for every arrival.

47
00:04:10.426 --> 00:04:15.227
It has been in place since late October.

48
00:04:15.227 --> 00:04:23.547
Borders and health, Ghana: Britain's Foreign Office says international arrivals should complete a health declaration and may face Ebola screening; that advice was already in force.

49
00:04:23.547 --> 00:04:30.217
Borders, Belize: the thirty-day state of emergency remains in force.

50
00:04:30.217 --> 00:04:36.326
Borders, Kenya: the Foreign Office still advises against all but essential travel to Moyale town and five kilometres around it.

51
00:04:36.326 --> 00:04:39.219
Hazards: Mayon volcano remains at alert level three.

52
00:04:39.219 --> 00:04:44.581
India's weather office again expects no depression to form in the next seven days.

53
00:04:44.581 --> 00:04:53.296
Infrastructure: Russian strikes left about six hundred thousand people without electricity in eastern Ukraine, reported via officials.

54
00:04:53.296 --> 00:04:54.982
That's today's brief.

55
00:04:54.982 --> 00:04:56.417
Current as of six a.m.

56
00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:59.110
Central, Sunday.

57
00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.566
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

58
00:05:01.566 --> 00:05:06.133
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

59
00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:08.522
Check the original source before you act.

60
00:05:08.522 --> 00:05:17.633
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

61
00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:20.298
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

62
00:05:20.298 --> 00:05:21.413
Thanks for listening.
